{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Run the inventory web application on node2, listening on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 directly served the inventory page and health endpoint on port 8080. After restart, Nginx was active and enabled, both IPv4 and IPv6 listeners were present, and the node2-specific application content remained available.","evidence_ids":["cmd-402c664907c347d3","cmd-89a913bb79d24291","cmd-3d599003a0584df7"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Run the inventory web application on node3, listening on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node3 directly served the inventory page and health endpoint on port 8080. After restart, Nginx was active and enabled, both listeners were present, and the node3-specific application content remained available.","evidence_ids":["cmd-91afb810694242d8","cmd-7d3a423d6538437a","cmd-78d3463aeb6946b0"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Configure node1 to load-balance incoming HTTP requests on port 80 across node2 and node3.","status":"satisfied","summary":"HAProxy was active and enabled on node1 with a port-80 listener. Repeated requests alternated between node2 and node3, and the final check confirmed both backends healthy and the inventory application available through node1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e0567d5795754464","cmd-96e7f287fab64c73","cmd-b5e4d201a65e4125","cmd-0bc0fd54ed7d42b7"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: installing the required servers, deploying application and load-balancer configuration, enabling/restarting services, and performing the mandatory restart protocol. No unnecessary troubleshooting mutations were identified. Package state remained consistent and no failed services were observed. Minor residue remained on node1: /tmp/post-node1-body and /tmp/final-body were bounded evidence artifacts but were not cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6e68432e63c34986","cmd-3472fb5ea6624b8e","cmd-a108e9abded24997","cmd-402c664907c347d3","cmd-91afb810694242d8","cmd-e0567d5795754464","cmd-81aff8897810461d","cmd-b424436efbfb4c9f","cmd-7475f518044a498e","cmd-dc96f28d7334464b","cmd-0bc0fd54ed7d42b7","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All three material outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also substantially complete for every node: each had a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/application state. Final traffic through node1 reached both recovered backends.","limitations":["The fixed after-executor boot-identity probe for node3 timed out, so it does not independently cross-check node3's restart. However, executor evidence directly records the boot ID changing from ac73b359-243e-418e-b7bb-a7cff423e597 to bf0cd541-2ac6-42c2-a516-9b142c70c3cb and shows recovered service, listener, health, and content state.","Lifecycle listening-socket snapshots were empty and therefore not useful for validating exposed ports; the port assertions instead rely on direct executor socket and HTTP observations."]}
